    "Every %lld in one set sees every %lld in the other, so %lld is in at most one of them. The set without %lld has as many digits as cells left, so it must hold all of them, %lld included.": {
      "comment": "Hint walkthrough page: ALS-XZ, the restricted common digit",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Every %1$lld in one set sees every %2$lld in the other, so %3$lld is in at most one of them. The set without %4$lld has as many digits as cells left, so it must hold all of them, %5$lld included."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bir kümedeki her %1$lld diğer kümedeki her %2$lld adayını görüyor; yani %3$lld en fazla birinde olabilir. %4$lld olmayan kümede hücre sayısı kadar rakam kalır, bu yüzden hepsini almak zorundadır; %5$lld de dahil."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Every empty cell has exactly two candidates except the cell at %@, which has three.": {
      "comment": "Hint walkthrough page: BUG+1 position",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Every empty cell has exactly two candidates except the cell at %@, which has three."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%1$@ hücresi dışındaki tüm boş hücrelerin tam iki adayı var; bu hücrenin üç adayı var."
          }
        }
      }
    },
